        "research": {
            "topic": "Posting frequency vs. reach: does volume beat quality on social media?",
            "summary": "Recent platform data shows feeds are now recommendation-driven and biased toward fresh content, and the largest public study on cadence found reach per post rises — not falls — as accounts post more often. Volume matters, but it compounds with format fit and consistency rather than replacing them.",
