            "keyPoints": [
                "The arithmetic in the script holds: 2–3x/week ≈ 130 posts/year, 2–3x/day ≈ 900/year — roughly a 7:1 volume gap.",
                "Buffer's 2.1M-post study found reach per post rose with frequency; accounts posting most often were not penalized.",
                "Consistency beat raw volume: highly consistent accounts earned far more engagement per post than sporadic ones.",
                "Feeds now favor recency — over half of recommended Instagram Feed content is less than a day old, double a year ago.",
                "TikTok ranks by interest, not follower count, so a new account can be surfaced widely on its first post.",
                "Hootsuite and Socialinsider benchmarks still put most brands' engagement sweet spot at 2–5 posts per week per platform, so volume is not a universal fix.",
                "No platform publishes official daily upload counts for TikTok — circulating '34 million/day' figures are third-party estimates, not verified data."
            ],
